diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
index 4479b53..2a44d2b 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -15,3 +15,26 @@ The application will now be running on `http://localhost:11224`.
 - **[React](https://react.dev/)**: Used for UI components.
 - **[Tailwind CSS](https://tailwindcss.com/)**: For styling the application.
 - **[Astro DB](https://docs.astro.build/en/guides/database/)**: Powers the comments feature, using a libSQL-compatible database.
+
+## Phone verification
+
+Sign-up now uses the local `api/signup/send`, `verify`, and `register` routes.
+Set `TWILIO_ACCOUNT_SID`, `TWILIO_AUTH_TOKEN`, and `TWILIO_VERIFY_SERVICE_SID`
+in the server environment (see `.env.example`). Configure the Twilio Verify service
+for six-digit SMS codes and enable its fraud protection and rate limits. Missing
+credentials return an unavailable message; no test codes bypass verification.
+
+For automatic SMS extraction, configure a domain-bound SMS template in Twilio
+with a final line like `@your-deployed-host.example #123456`, substituting the
+actual code and the exact host serving sign-up (no scheme or path). WebOTP needs
+HTTPS and a supported browser; `autocomplete="one-time-code"`, paste, and manual
+entry are also supported. See [WebOTP documentation](https://developer.chrome.com/docs/identity/web-apis/web-otp)
+and [Twilio Verify](https://www.twilio.com/docs/verify/api).
+
+Verification expires after ten minutes, allows five local code attempts, and
+limits resends to once per minute per session. Use a shared Astro session store
+for multi-instance deployments and configure provider-level rate limits for
+cross-session SMS abuse. The local registration route requires a verified session
+and forwards the verified `phoneNumber` to the existing registration service.
+That external service must also enforce verification for any direct registration
+clients; its implementation is outside this repository.
